Subject: [PATCH] rtl8xxxu: wait longer for the beacon valid bit

After clearing BCN_VALID and sending the new beacon, the driver polled
the bit for only ~1-2ms. The beacon goes through the same USB bulk
endpoint as the other frames, so under load (e.g. a station loading a
web page) it reaches the chip later and "Failed to read beacon valid
bit" was logged every few seconds on the RTL8188EU, even though the
beacon was eventually loaded.

Poll for up to ~20ms (100 x 100-200us), still well below the beacon
interval. The function runs from a workqueue, so sleeping is fine.

Applies on top of 0003.
---
--- a/rtl8xxxu_core.c
+++ b/rtl8xxxu_core.c
@@ -5695,16 +5695,24 @@
 	if (skb)
 		rtl8xxxu_tx(hw, NULL, skb);
 
+	/*
+	 * The beacon shares the USB bulk endpoint with the other frames, so
+	 * under load it can reach the chip several ms later: wait up to
+	 * ~20ms (the beacon interval is ~100ms) instead of ~2ms.
+	 */
 	retry = 100;
 	do {
 		val8 = rtl8xxxu_read8(priv, REG_TDECTRL + 2);
 		if (val8 & (BIT_BCN_VALID >> 16))
 			break;
-		usleep_range(10, 20);
+		usleep_range(100, 200);
 	} while (--retry);
 
 	if (!retry)
 		dev_err(dev, "%s: Failed to read beacon valid bit\n", __func__);
+	else if (retry < 90)
+		dev_dbg(dev, "%s: beacon valid after %d polls\n", __func__,
+			100 - retry);
 }
 
 static void rtl8xxxu_update_beacon_work_callback(struct work_struct *work)
